<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Trust can end before access does.</h1>
    <p class="sub">Accounts set up for a shared life can outlast it. Dr. Lior Tabansky finds, with you and in person, what still connects you.</p>
    {% include "founder.njk" %}
    {% include "hero-actions.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head"><span class="sec__no">01</span><span class="label">Recognition</span></div>
    <div class="sec__body">
      <h2>Choose which access you keep.</h2>
      <ul class="ruled">
        <li>A family cloud that still shares photos and documents.</li>
        <li>A recovery number or email that belongs to your spouse.</li>
        <li>An old phone or tablet still signed in to your messages.</li>
        <li>Location sharing set up years ago.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of it you still need. Dr. Tabansky shows you what each connection allows, so you can tell access you want to keep from access you want to end.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec__head"><span class="sec__no">02</span><span class="label">Sequence</span></div>
    <div class="sec__body">
      <h2>Change things in the right order.</h2>
      <p class="lede">A password change can leave another route open, and changing a family service can cut access you rely on. You agree the sequence together before anything changes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="how-it-works">
